[5.071629, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[4D\u001b[25B\r\u001b[2C\u001b[23A\u001b[38;5;153mibi-\u001b[8Gsk        \u001b[38GAnswer\u001b[45Ga free-text\u001b[57Gengin\u001b[63Gering question from the Kes\u001b[91Gra archit\u001b[101Gcture\u001b[107GKB.\u001b[111GU\u001b[114G when the\u001b[124Guser runs\u001b[134G`/kibi-ask <questio\u001b[154G>` or asks\r\u001b[37C\u001b[1Ban\u001b[41Ga\u001b[43Gchitectu\u001b[52Ge / \"how does X work\" question the engineering wiki should answer. Dispatches the kibi-eng-answerer sub-agent (…\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1Bk\u001b[38;5;246mibi-lint                  \u001b[39Gh\u001b[41Gc\u001b[38;5;153mk\u001b[38;5;246m and\u001b[48Gauto-fix integrity of the Kestra KB vault — broken\u001b[99Gwikil\u001b[105Gnk\u001b[110Gstal\u001b[115G index cells,\u001b[129GTOC drift, category memb\u001b[154Grship,\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[37C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246mg\u001b[40Gaph c\u001b[46Glors. Use\u001b[56Gw\u001b[61Gt\u001b[64G user runs `/\u001b[38;5;153mk\u001b[79G\u001b[38;5;246mbi-lint` or\u001b[91Gasks\u001b[96Gto lint/validate/check the vault, find broken links, or verify the …\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;153mk\u001b[38;5;246mibi-design       \u001b[38GCo-author a \u001b[38;5;153mK\u001b[38;5;246mestra Improvement Proposal (KIP) by brainstorming a target architecture i\u001b[126Geractively, grou\u001b[143Gded in \u001b[151Ghe\r\u001b[37C\u001b[1Bengi\u001b[43Geering \u001b[38;5;153mK\u001b[38;5;246mB. Use when the user runs `/kib\u001b[83G-design <topic>` or asks to draft/write a KIP, brainstorm an architecture, or de…\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;153mk\u001b[4G\u001b[38;5;246mybindings        \u001b[38GOp\u001b[41Gn your \u001b[38;5;153mk\u001b[38;5;246meyboard shortcuts file\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m/\u001b[38;5;153mk\u001b[38;5;246mibi-eng-reorg                      R\u001b[40Gorganize th\u001b[52G \u001b[38;5;153mK\u001b[55G\u001b[38;5;246mst\u001b[58Ga engineering a\u001b[74Gchitecture KB into categories. Use when the user runs `/kibi-eng-reorg` or asks to\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m                                     \u001b[38;5;246mcate\u001b[43Gorize scopes, regenerate\u001b[68Gcategory pages, or\u001b[87Grebuild\u001b[95Gthe top-level index cat\u001b[119Ggories/scopes tables. Dispatches the \u001b[38;5;153mk\u001b[38;5;246mibi-en…\r\u001b[1B/\u001b[38;5;153mk\u001b[38;5;246mibi-eng-update                     Refre\u001b[44Gh or\u001b[49Gbootstrap a \u001b[38;5;153mK\u001b[38;5;246me\u001b[64Gtra engineering architec\u001b[89Gure knowledge base page in an\u001b[119GObsidian\u001b[128Gvault. Use when the user runs\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B                                     \u001b[38;5;246m`/\u001b[38;5;153mk\u001b[38;5;246mibi-\u001b[46Gng-update\u001b[56G<scope>` or asks to refresh the engineering architecture KB for a scope (e.g. RBAC, AI Copilot, Worker, Exe…\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;153mk\u001b[38;5;246mestra-plugin-qa\u001b[38GBuild, deploy, and\u001b[57Gbrowser-test a \u001b[38;5;153mK\u001b[38;5;246mes\u001b[76Gra plugin end-to-end. Use when the user asks to QA, test, or validate a plugin, issue,\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m                                     \u001b[38;5;246mor branch. (pr\u001b[53Gject)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;153mk\u001b[38;5;246mestra-plugin-plan\u001b[38GRead a GitHub issue, generat\u001b[67G a s\u001b[72Gructured implementation plan, and post it as a comment. Human must then comment\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m                                     \u001b[38;5;246m/plan-approved before implementation can b\u001b[81Ggin. (project)\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;153mk\u001b[38;5;246mestra-plugin-issue\u001b[38GEx\u001b[41Gcute full end-to-end implementation of a\u001b[82G\u001b[38;5;153mK\u001b[38;5;246mes\u001b[86Gra plugin GitHub issue. Requires /plan-approved comment to exist. Orchestrates\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m                                     \u001b[38;5;246mdeveloper +\u001b[50Greviewer + QA\u001b[64G+ docs d\u001b[73Grectly. (project)\u0